  <text xml:base="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0443.bakchai.meineke1839-grc1" xml:lang="grc"><body n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0443.bakchai.meineke1839-grc1" xml:lang="grc"><div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0443.bakchai.meineke1839-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0443_bakchai"><head>ΒΑΚΧΑΙ</head><div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="i" author_heading="DIOCLES." work_heading="ΒΑΚΧΑΙ" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0443-bakchai-i">
              <label>I.</label>
              <lg>
                <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0443-bakchai-i-l1">Ὑδρία τις ἢ χαλκοῦς ποδανιπτὴρ ἢ λέβης.</l>
              </lg>
              <note type="source">Pollux X 78: καλεῖται μέντοι ποδανιπτὴρ οὐ παρ' Ἡροδότῳ (II 172) μόνον ἀλλὰ καὶ ἐν Διοκλέους Βάκχαις <lg>
                  <l n="1_2" xml:id="meineke-0443-bakchai-i-l1_2">Ὑδρία τις κτλ.</l>
                </lg>
              </note>
              <note type="apparatus">Particulam ἢ ante λέβης addidere Bentleius Epist. ad Hemsterh. p. 99 et Toupius Emend. III p. 101.</note>
            </div>
            <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="ii" author_heading="DIOCLES." work_heading="ΒΑΚΧΑΙ" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0443-bakchai-ii">
              <label>II.</label>
              <lg>
                <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0443-bakchai-ii-l1">Πλυνεῖ τε τὰ κακὰ τῶν κακῶν ὑμᾶς.</l>
              </lg>
              <note type="source">Photius p. 124 17. Κακὰ κακῶν: Διοκλῆς Βάκχη (sic) <lg>
                  <l n="1_2" xml:id="meineke-0443-bakchai-ii-l1_2">Πλυνεῖ τε τὰ κακὰ τῶν κακῶν ὑμᾶς.</l>
                </lg> Eadem Suidas s. v. κακὰ κακῶν, ubi Dioclis verba vitiose scripta sunt hoc modo: <lg>
                  <l n="1_3" xml:id="meineke-0443-bakchai-ii-l1_3">Πλυνεῖ τε κακὰ τῶν κακῶν ὑμᾶς.</l>
                </lg>
              </note>
              <note type="apparatus">Cfr Elmsleius ad Sophoclis Oed. Col. p. 260. De dictione τῶν κακῶν τὰ κακὰ et similibus exempla attuli Hist. crit. p. 69. In fine versus Th. Bergkius Comment. p. 429 addebat κακῶς.</note>
            </div>
            <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="iii" author_heading="DIOCLES." work_heading="ΒΑΚΧΑΙ" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0443-bakchai-iii">
              <label>III.</label>
              <note type="source">Antiatticista p. 87 2: Γυναικισμός. Διοκλῆς Βάκχαις γυναικίζειν φησὶ καὶ γυναικηρόν.</note>
              <note type="apparatus">Fortasse γυναικισμόν.</note>
            </div>
          <pb n="839" facs="urn:hathi:hvd.hxjhbd:scan:857" />
            <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="iv" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0443-bakchai-iv">
              <head>IV.</head>
              <note type="source">Grammaticus Bekkeri Anecd. p. 452 28. <quote>Ἀσκοθύλακος: Διοκλῆς Βάκχαις καὶ ῎Αρχιππος Ἀμφιτρύωνι δευτέρῳ.</quote>
              </note>
              <note type="apparatus">Habet etiam Aristophanes Fragm. 217.</note>
            </div>
          </div></body></text></TEI>